{
  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that has begun collecting node contents. Further node inputs can be added before awaiting the answer.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct NodePhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.NodePhase` says a request in this phase has begun collecting node contents and that more node inputs can be added before the answer is awaited.\n\n- **Entering the phase.** `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` starts with `ctx.ask().context(..).contents_of_current_node()`. `task_messages_share_a_prefix_and_can_queue_another_node` enters it through `contents_of_node(selected)` and annotates the result with the type `crate::request::Ask<.., NodePhase>`. That annotation checks the phase marker at compile time.\n- **Adding more inputs.** The first test chains `contents_of_successors(7)` and a second `contents_of_current_node()` onto a request already in the node phase. It asserts the exact request inputs in order, including the repeated nodes. It also asserts the reads and the recorded dependencies.\n- **Awaiting from the phase.** The first test awaits the request directly with `into_future()` and checks the answer. The second test finishes the request with `.message(task)` and awaits it twice, then checks the messages, the shared prefix and the inputs.\n\nThe tests exercise the obligations the text states and assert their outcomes. Public export of `NodePhase` is covered by `public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs`, which is marked for `requirements.sdk.public_api` rather than for this requirement. I found no gap.",
